<article class="env-remark" id="061D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/061D">Remark <span data-tag="061D">76.17.6</span>.</a> A special case of Lemmas <a href="/tag/0618" data-tag="0618">76.17.1</a>, <a href="/tag/04D0" data-tag="04D0">76.17.2</a>, <a href="/tag/061A" data-tag="061A">76.17.4</a>, and <a href="/tag/061C" data-tag="061C">76.17.5</a> is where $Y = Y'$. In this case the map $A$ is always zero. The sheaf of Lemma <a href="/tag/061A" data-tag="061A">76.17.4</a> is just given by the rule </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  U' \mapsto \{ a' : U' \to Y\text{ over }B\text{ with } a'|_ U = a|_ U\}   \]
</div>
  <p> and we act on this by the sheaf $\mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{O}_ X}(a^*\Omega _{Y/B}, \mathcal{C}_{X/X'})$. </p>
</article>